@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Address lookup";
}

<span class="govuk-caption-xl">Example application</span>

<div class="govuk-grid-row govuk-grid-row--tpr-divider">
    <div class="govuk-grid-column govuk-grid-column-full">
        <h1 class="govuk-heading-l">@ViewData["Title"]</h1>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="govuk-grid-row">
    <div class="govuk-grid-column govuk-grid-column-two-thirds-from-desktop">
        <govuk-warning-text icon-fallback-text="Warning">
            This component relies on JavaScript to allow its full functionality.
        </govuk-warning-text>
        <p class="govuk-body">
            The address lookup component can be added to any page where you want the user to be able to search for an address.
        </p>
        <p class="govuk-body">
            Given a postcode and a building name or number the <a class="govuk-link" href="https://www.ordnancesurvey.co.uk/products/os-places-api" target="_blank">Ordnance Survey Places API</a> is 
            queried using the postcode endpoint. Results are then filtered by the building name or number. If an exact match is found, the user is taken to the 'confirmed' view. If more than one result is found, 
            the user must select an address and is then taken to the 'confirmed' view.
        </p>
        <p class="govuk-body">
            The 'confirmed' view populates hidden inputs with values, including the UPRN.
        </p>
        <p class="govuk-body">
            The user also has the option to manually enter a UK or international address.
        </p>
        <p class="govuk-body">
            The JavaScript file <strong>'address-lookup/index.js'</strong> is provided as part of the <strong>'ThePensionsRegulator.Frontend'</strong> NuGet package. This must be included in any view that uses this component.
        </p>

        <govuk-inset-text>
            &ltscript src="~/_Content/ThePensionsRegulator.Frontend/tpr/address-lookup/index.js" type="module"&gt;&lt;script&gt;
        </govuk-inset-text>

        <p class="govuk-body">
            If JavaScript is not available then the component will display input fields for entering an international address. The labels
            for these fields can be customised.
        </p>

        <p class="govuk-body">
            Use the <strong>'tpr-address-lookup-legend'</strong> tag helper to add a legend to the fieldset.
            The legend will be rendered as a proper <code>&lt;legend&gt;</code> element with the <code>govuk-fieldset__legend</code> class applied.
        </p>

        <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">
            Customising labels and error messages
        </h2>

        <p class="govuk-body">
            Labels and validation error messages can be customised in three ways, listed here in priority order:
        </p>

        <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
            <li>
                <strong>Server-rendered inputs</strong> &ndash; The component captures the label text, required message, max length,
                and pattern message from any <code>&lt;input&gt;</code> or <code>&lt;select&gt;</code> elements rendered inside the
                <code>&lt;tpr-address-lookup&gt;</code> element. These are used when JavaScript rebuilds the component.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong><code>data-*</code> attributes on the container</strong> &ndash; For fields that only exist in JavaScript
                (building name, UK postcode for the search view, county, and select address), you can set <code>data-address-lookup-{field}-{property}</code>
                attributes on the <code>&lt;tpr-address-lookup&gt;</code> element. For example,
                <code>data-address-lookup-postcode-label</code> or <code>data-address-lookup-building-maxlength</code>.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Built-in defaults</strong> &ndash; If no value is provided by either of the above methods, the component
                falls back to default values defined in <code>config.js</code>.
            </li>
        </ol>

        <p class="govuk-body">
            The available <code>data-*</code> attributes for JavaScript-only fields are:
        </p>

        <govuk-details>
            <govuk-details-summary>data-* attributes for JavaScript-only fields</govuk-details-summary>
            <govuk-details-text>
                <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
                    <li><code>data-address-lookup-postcode-label</code></li>
                    <li><code>data-address-lookup-postcode-required</code></li>
                    <li><code>data-address-lookup-postcode-maxlength</code></li>
                    <li><code>data-address-lookup-postcode-pattern</code></li>
                    <li><code>data-address-lookup-building-label</code></li>
                    <li><code>data-address-lookup-building-maxlength</code></li>
                    <li><code>data-address-lookup-county-label</code></li>
                    <li><code>data-address-lookup-county-maxlength</code></li>
                    <li><code>data-address-lookup-select-address-label</code></li>
                    <li><code>data-address-lookup-select-address-required</code></li>
                </ul>
            </govuk-details-text>
        </govuk-details>

        <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">
            Primary and secondary address lookup components
        </h2>

        <p class="govuk-body">
            An address lookup component can be configured to be a primary or secondary component. It defaults to primary.
        </p>

        <p class="govuk-body">
            If the component is configured to be secondary, a checkbox is displayed which, when checked, puts that component in the 'confirmed' view with the same address as the primary component.
        </p>

        <p class="govuk-body">
            The secondary component expects the primary component to appear first on the page.
        </p>

        <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">
            Configuration
        </h2>

        <p class="govuk-body">
            Two URLs are required to be configured to allow this component to search for addresses.
        </p>

        <h3 class="govuk-heading-s">
            SearchEndpoint
        </h3>

        <p class="govuk-body">
            This should be the URL for the <a class="govuk-link" href="https://docs.os.uk/os-apis/accessing-os-apis/os-places-api/technical-specification/postcode" target="_blank">postcode endpoint</a> of the Ordnance Survey API,
            or an equivalent service.
        </p>

        <h3 class="govuk-heading-s">
            AddressByIdEndpoint
        </h3>

        <p class="govuk-body">
            This should be the URL for the <a class="govuk-link" href="https://docs.os.uk/os-apis/accessing-os-apis/os-places-api/technical-specification/uprn" target="_blank">postcode endpoint</a> of the Ordnance Survey API,
            or an equivalent service.
        </p>

        <p class="govuk-body">
            These are configured via <strong>appsettings.json</strong> under a section name <strong>AddressLookup</strong>.
        </p>

        <govuk-inset-text>
<pre><code>"AddressLookup": { 
    "SearchEndpoint": "https://api.os.uk/search/places/v1/postcode",
    "AddressByIdEndpoint": "https://api.os.uk/search/places/v1/uprn"
}</code></pre>
        </govuk-inset-text>

        <govuk-warning-text icon-fallback-text="Warning">
            Consuming services must implement ITprCountryRepository to allow this component's full functionality.
        </govuk-warning-text>

        <p class="govuk-body">
            To allow the 'manual international view' to show a select input of countries, consuming services must implement ITprCountryRepository.
        </p>

        <hr class="govuk-section-break govuk-section-break--visible govuk-section-break--m" />

        <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Address lookup examples</h2>

        <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
            <li>
                <a class="govuk-link" asp-controller="AddressLookup" asp-action="NoDataProvided">No data provided</a>
            </li>
            <li>
                <a class="govuk-link" asp-controller="AddressLookup" asp-action="PrimaryDataProvided">Primary address data provided</a>
            </li>
            <li>
                <a class="govuk-link" asp-controller="AddressLookup" asp-action="PrimaryAndSecondaryDataProvided">Primary and secondary data provided</a>
            </li>
            <li>
                <a class="govuk-link" asp-controller="AddressLookup" asp-action="JavaScriptDisabled">JavaScript disabled</a>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>